#X text 20 20 Was u_oled-preview.pd. It is a SUBPATCH now \, not an abstraction \, because the eight screen rows live on the panel above and \$0- names do not cross an abstraction boundary -- a subpatch shares its parent's \$0 \, which is exactly what is needed., f 58;
#X text 700 20 Eight rows \, one per 8-pixel row of the 128x64 screen \, keyed by the y coordinate of each drawing command. It shows WHAT is drawn and roughly where -- a 24px line covers three rows but only registers in the one it starts in., f 58;
#X obj 20 240 r oscOut;
#X obj 20 280 route sendtyped;
#X obj 900 330 print oscOut-not-sendtyped;
#X obj 20 330 route /oled/gPrintln /oled/gClear /oled/gFillArea /oled/gFlip /oled/gShowInfoBar /oled/gBox;
#X obj 1780 410 print oscOut-unhandled;
#X text 1780 460 gShowInfoBar and gBox are routed and DELIBERATELY left unconnected: both go out on every frame and would drown the console. Swallowing them by name is what keeps this reject print worth having -- it now only fires for a command this previewer has never seen., f 28;
