#X text 20 600 EXACTLY ONE OUTPUT PER INPUT. The accumulator emits on every iteration \, so without the spigot a three-word row would redraw the screen three times and log three lines. The gate is shut before the loop and opened for one deliberate re-emit afterwards., f 46;
#X text 20 740 The counter runs UP \, 0 to n-1 \, because list prepend puts its RIGHT inlet first: accumulator \, then the new word. Running it down silently reverses every row -- which is exactly what the first version did., f 46;
#X text 20 880 route float catches a value that never got stringified and sends it through makefilename %g. list fromsymbol has no method for a float and would otherwise stop the row dead., f 46;
#X text 20 1020 The four \$0- sends carry the signals that would otherwise be long cords across three lanes. Local \, inside one abstraction \, and the alternative is a diagram nobody can read., f 46;
