#X text 20 1350 The row number is stashed in an f while the join runs \, then banged back out to pack once the joined symbol has arrived in the cold inlet. Pd is synchronous \, so the join always returns before the next row arrives -- one instance serves all eight., f 58;
#X text 620 1350 gFillArea's width in pixels became a bar back in g_oled? No -- the bar is drawn HERE. See pd bar in the parent: 21 characters \, n of = and the rest of - \, so the two channels can be compared at a glance., f 58;
#X text 1220 1350 gClear walks 0 to 7 through the same router the drawing commands use \, blanking every row. With four layers a leftover row is a lie about which layer is showing., f 58;
#N canvas 40 40 1200 900 bar 0;
#X text 20 20 A gFillArea width in pixels becomes a 21-character bar: n of = then 21-n of -. FIXED width on purpose -- a bar that resizes its own box is much harder to compare against the one above it \, and comparing the two channels is the entire point of the home screen., f 58;
